menu "BTClock diagnostics"

config BTCLOCK_HEAP_INTEGRITY_INTERVAL_MS
    int "Heap integrity check interval (ms)"
    range 1000 3600000
    default 30000
    help
      How often the periodic heap integrity check task calls
      heap_caps_check_integrity_all(). Detects allocator-metadata
      corruption shortly after it happens so the coredump captures
      the live state at the corruption site, instead of the
      secondary-victim panic that lands later when an unrelated
      allocator call hits the damaged arena.

      30 s (default) walks ~300 allocator blocks in ~1-2 ms — about
      0.005 % CPU. Tighten for active corruption hunts (e.g. 5000
      ms), loosen for production soaks where the cost should be
      effectively zero (e.g. 300000).

      Pair with CONFIG_HEAP_POISONING_LIGHT (or COMPREHENSIVE) under
      "Component config → Heap memory debugging" for finer-grained
      corruption detection — without poisoning, the integrity walk
      only catches allocator-arena damage, not adjacent-block stomp
      bugs.

      See bd btclock_v4-28n for the original httpd-task crash trail
      this monitor was added to catch.

endmenu
